WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.450
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit
6: Describing People and Things.

2
00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:09.189
Here you learn how to describe
people and things with precise words.

3
00:00:09.269 --> 00:00:15.879
You collect words for what somebody is like
inside, such as kind, honest, friendly and careless,

4
00:00:15.959 --> 00:00:21.732
and words for what things are like outside,
such as rough, tough, similar and alive.

5
00:00:21.812 --> 00:00:27.865
You compare two people with kinder and busier,
you tell true stories in the past simple,

6
00:00:27.945 --> 00:00:31.628
and you use could to say what somebody was able to do.

7
00:00:31.708 --> 00:00:39.433
Along the way you read about Amal, a new girl who discovers
that carrying kindness makes everybody feel welcome.

8
00:00:39.513 --> 00:00:45.287
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:53.339
By the end of this unit, you will be able to use describing
words (adjectives) to talk about people and things.

10
00:00:53.419 --> 00:00:58.924
You will also describe your favourite
person and say what makes them special.

11
00:00:59.004 --> 00:01:05.089
You will also compare two people or things,
using words like kinder and rougher than.

12
00:01:05.169 --> 00:01:07.773
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:07.853 --> 00:01:13.426
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
kind, friendly, honest, kindness, care, busy.

14
00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:18.457
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:18.537 --> 00:01:22.370
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:25.855
The reading sequence includes My Cousin Noah and Two Roads.

17
00:01:25.935 --> 00:01:26.682
Read actively.

18
00:01:26.762 --> 00:01:30.759
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:30.839 --> 00:01:34.599
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:34.679 --> 00:01:38.000
The first language focus is The Past Simple Tense.

21
00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:42.489
We use the past simple to talk
about things that already happened.

22
00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:48.883
It helps us tell stories and describe what people
did, like Nora, who helped the boy who fell.

23
00:01:48.963 --> 00:01:56.296
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:01:56.376 --> 00:02:00.987
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1 — Describe Your Favourite Person.

25
00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:05.177
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:05.257 --> 00:02:08.367
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:08.447 --> 00:02:11.682
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:11.762 --> 00:02:13.232
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:13.312 --> 00:02:19.903
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:19.983 --> 00:02:23.138
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:23.218 --> 00:02:30.618
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
